# PowerShell 5.1 reads a script with no BOM as the system ANSI code page
# (GBK on Chinese Windows). Keep the UTF-8 BOM in the blob.
# `text eol=crlf` only normalizes newlines; it does not re-encode, so the BOM stays.
# Do not set working-tree-encoding (including UTF-16): that re-encodes and drops the BOM.
# `-text` would also keep the raw bytes, but it skips newline normalization.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
